From 8ec6fd87a5ab7625e53a419a56b1c6d4e8051ce3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:23:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] kubelet: record the pod jail's limits when the sandbox
 is created, not on every sync

generatePodSandboxConfig (and so applySandboxResources) runs on every pod
sync, from the pod's desired resources. Recording the 'applied' pod-level
config there made it equal the desired one just before the resize compared
them, so the kubelet never sent UpdatePodSandboxResources: the pod jail
kept its old limits (seen live: pod resized 200Mi -> 500Mi, containers
updated, pod jail still 200Mi). Record it from the config the runtime
created the sandbox with (new sandboxCreated hook, a no-op on other
platforms). Regression test.
